--- doc/exec.n
+++ doc/exec.n
@@ -204,10 +204,17 @@
 The standard output from the last command in the pipeline will
 go to the application's standard output if it has not been
 redirected, and error output from all of
 the commands in the pipeline will go to the application's
 standard error file unless redirected.
+Files named in redirections are opened by \fBexec\fR itself before it
+returns, so that errors in them can be reported. If such an open blocks,
+for example on a named pipe (FIFO) that nobody has opened for the other
+direction yet, \fBexec\fR blocks too, even with
+.QW & .
+Let a shell open the file in that case, as in
+\fBexec sh -c {cat <fifo} &\fR.
 .PP
 The first word in each command is taken as the command name;
 if the result contains
 no slashes then the directories
 in the PATH environment variable are searched for

